{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"431d509d9edf02e6bf27248dfb0edb7d949a6f69fe837d514babe2d734e64d52","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T18:33:28Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_recovered_from":"1abb1526239d5f30092c7215c45e447eb4bd47435f656b24b07b61f8eee89a99","anchor_verified":true,"mapped_intervals":[[88,88]],"mapped_path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","quoted_text":"      if (process.platform !== 'win32' && dirname(source) === resolve(installed, '.bin')) {","reason":"`fs.promises.cp` passes the filter `source` using the path form supplied to `cp`. When `installed` is relative, `dirname(source)` remains relative while `resolve(installed, '.bin')` is absolute, so the `.bin` branch is skipped and the shim isolation described on lines 85-87 is lost. The same function already resolves `source` on line 91 when writing the launcher, confirming relative source paths are otherwise handled. Resolving `dirname(source)` in the comparison fixes the mismatch.","recovered_anchor":{"anchor_recovered_from":"1abb1526239d5f30092c7215c45e447eb4bd47435f656b24b07b61f8eee89a99","blob":"13e395590f70d45b4a2af4909e5c638430e4ddb5","intervals":[[88,88]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts"},"target":"86247bb624de9ef20453df5d66ce9ef84040f933"},"finding_id":"c967cecca8296384ff6d948843fde9b3ea94dacae7413c6713c0804661ea60a8","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"25b1906859ffc9785e8a975893547702dae359e97524d87faba7fae11c8eaadf"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:c967cecca8296384ff6d948843fde9b3ea94dacae7413c6713c0804661ea60a8:51927e1b0c78fad7241701802d377b268a103a06171cda71682fec0b2a6743f5"}